# the startup splash (TUI-DESIGN-2 §5; TUI-DESIGN-3 §3 D-I): the first frame is splash frame 0 with the `step 0/–` sentinel; a key at
# ~100 ms completes the reveal instead of killing it — the resting mark is COMMITTED as the first scrollback block (the owner's directive
# of 2026-09-23) and no later frame draws it in the dynamic region (no `▓▒░` head after the echo frame); the idle frame is 6 dynamic rows
# (the rule and the console); zero clears (§8.2 splash.steps, round 3)
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect step 0/
# raw mode on (Ink's post-commit effect writes ESC[?2004h): a key sent earlier is a cooked-mode byte the kernel echoes
expect \x1b\[\?2004h
sleep 0.1
send h
expect (?:›|>) (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*h
sleep 0.3
send \x03
expect Say hi
expect sess \$
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
